  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Bound Report Shelf",
    "overview": "PRO is the department's shelf of bound final-year reports, filed by academic year. The shell is maroon bookcloth: a 60px top bar on desktop and a cloth drawer on narrow screens. Everything you read sits on cool report paper as white sheets with hairline rules. Gold foil is scarce. It marks identity (the wordmark, the role stamp, foil-stamped titles) and the current place (the active-tab rule). The signature object is the year shelf: one spine per project, bound in its status colour, standing on a wooden ledge and grouped by academic year.\n\nThe system is dense and data-first. Tables, chips and records do the work, and ornament is limited to the materials of a bound report: cloth, foil, paper, ledge. Three borrowed devices hold it together. Each entity family has one fixed hue wherever it appears. Hovering a relation lights the rows it touches and dims the rest. Every number is set in tabular monospace. The world rejects the white-sidebar, KPI-card admin template. No sidebar, no stat tiles, no gradient hero.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Bookcloth shell (top bar, drawer, login cloth panel, toast) over a cool report-paper ground.",
      "Foil gold reserved for identity marks and the current place.",
      "Status shown as binding colour, always paired with its word.",
      "One hue per entity family, carried by chips and hue marks.",
      "Tabular monospace numerals for IDs, years and scores.",
      "Relation hover lights the related rows and spines and dims the rest."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Foil Is Earned Rule",
        "body": "Gold appears as type only on cloth: the wordmark, the login headline, the role stamp and spine titles. On paper it appears only as a rule or a frame (the active tab, the certificate border, status caps), plus the skip link's foil plate with cloth-deep text. Never use it as running text on paper.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Binding Is Status Rule",
        "body": "The four binding colours mean project status and nothing else. A binding colour never appears without its word next to it or a legend beside it.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Hue Per Family Rule",
        "body": "An entity family keeps its hue everywhere. Projects are maroon, teams green, people navy, subjects (domains, technologies, categories) ochre and evaluations violet. Never use a family hue for decoration or for a different family.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Foil Type Rule",
        "body": "Caslon is only for the wordmark, the login headline and certificate titles. Never use it for a page title, a section head or UI chrome.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tabular Rule",
        "body": "Any number a reader compares (ID, year, score, count) is set in the mono with tabular figures and right-aligned in numeric columns.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Only Things That Lift Are Books Rule",
        "body": "Only shelf objects move off the plane. Sheets, chips and buttons stay flat. A button's only press feedback is a 1px drop.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** build every new surface on paper, with white sheets (8px radius, rule border, Sheet shadow) and cloth only for the shell.",
      "**Do** pair every binding colour with its status word, using the status mark or the shelf legend.",
      "**Do** colour any reference to a project, team, person, subject or evaluation with that family's hue, as a chip or a hue mark.",
      "**Do** set IDs, years, scores and counts in Atkinson Hyperlegible Mono with tabular figures.",
      "**Do** light related rows and spines on relation hover, and dim the rest.",
      "**Do** show validation errors under the field, in danger text with an icon."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** build the white-sidebar, KPI-card admin template. Navigation lives in the cloth bar, and the repository opens on the shelf.",
      "**Don't** set gold foil as text on paper. On paper it is a rule or a frame (the skip link's plate is the one fill).",
      "**Don't** use Libre Caslon Display outside the wordmark, the login headline and certificate titles.",
      "**Don't** use a binding colour for anything except status, or a family hue for anything except its family.",
      "**Don't** lift sheets, chips or buttons with shadows. Only shelf objects leave the plane.",
      "**Don't** warm the ground to cream. Report paper stays cool."
    ]
